### VS Code REST Client file. Fill variables, run each request, screenshot response -> docs/evidence/
@api = http://localhost:3000
@studentToken = PASTE_STUDENT_TOKEN
@adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN
@auditorToken = PASTE_AUDITOR_TOKEN
@electionId = PASTE_ELECTION_UUID

### ST-01 unauthenticated -> 401
GET {{api}}/api/elections/{{electionId}}/turnout

### ST-02 unauthorized role: student creates election -> 403
POST {{api}}/api/elections
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Hack","start_time":"2030-01-01T10:00:00Z","end_time":"2030-01-01T14:00:00Z"}

### ST-02b admin reads audit log -> 403 (separation of duties)
GET {{api}}/api/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ST-04 invalid input -> 400 (end before start)
POST {{api}}/api/elections
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Bad dates","start_time":"2030-01-01T14:00:00Z","end_time":"2030-01-01T10:00:00Z"}

### ST-04b mass assignment ignored (created_by/status not accepted from body)
POST {{api}}/api/elections
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Mass assign test","start_time":"2030-01-01T10:00:00Z","end_time":"2030-01-01T14:00:00Z","status":"OPEN","created_by":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"}

### ST-05 SQL injection attempt in id -> 400
GET {{api}}/api/elections/1'%20OR%20'1'='1/turnout
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ST-10 tampered token -> 401
GET {{api}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJub25lIiwidHlwIjoiSldUIn0.eyJzdWIiOiJhZG1pbiIsInJvbGUiOiJBRE1JTiJ9.

### ST-11 brute force: send this 6 times with a wrong password -> 401 x5 then 423
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"student1@example.edu","password":"wrong-password-123","turnstileToken":"XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN"}

### ST-17 CORS from evil origin -> no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header
OPTIONS {{api}}/api/elections
Origin: http://evil.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
